# Numbered workflow dirs (N_CAPSNAME: 0_TODO, 0_OVERNIGHT_WORK, 1_REVIEW, 2_ARTIFACTS, ...):
# local async handoff / scratch between Mark & Claude, mostly not tracked.
# Tracked exceptions: workflow history files (backed up in git for disaster recovery)
#
# ORDER MATTERS, twice over:
#  1. The catch-all must match at ANY depth (no leading slash) -- these dirs live under vck5000/.
#     The leading slash added by the MARK_TO_REVIEW -> REVIEW rename stopped it matching
#     vck5000/1_REVIEW and vck5000/2_ARTIFACTS, which then sat untracked-but-NOT-ignored,
#     including ~80 MB of GIFs that a `git add -A` would have swept in.
#  2. It must come BEFORE the 0_TODO exceptions. git does not descend into an excluded
#     DIRECTORY, so a re-include of a file inside one can never fire -- the negation has to
#     win on the directory itself, which means appearing later in the file.
[0-9]_*/
!/vck5000/0_TODO/
/vck5000/0_TODO/*
!/vck5000/0_TODO/history.md
!/vck5000/0_TODO/TODO.md
vck5000/host/benchmarks/mms/
